# THE KEPT-BY SHELF (docs/GEAR.md §7, G6, KeptBy): a room somebody lives in
# (InteriorKind.seats) keeps what it holds on one of its own pieces, and it is
# theirs. A stranger is told so and takes nothing; once the region has thanked
# the player for an ask he answered (`thanked` stages it), it is given, once.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/kept_by.tour --seed=4 --hour=15 --weather=clear:0
#
# 01 is a coast cottage's shelf to a stranger: nothing taken. 02 is the same
# shelf once the region has thanked him: what they gave. 03-11 are every other
# lived-in kind, each at its own shelf as it is given.
coast calm
near door:cottage
await door 5
press use 0.1
await inside:cottage 5
wait 0.6
near shelf
wait 0.4
press use 0.1
await shelf_theirs 3
wait 0.6
shot 01-a-cottage-shelf-is-theirs with inside:cottage,shelf_near
thanked
wait 0.3
press use 0.1
await shelf_given 3
wait 0.6
shot 02-given-for-what-he-did with inside:cottage
near door
wait 0.3
press use 0.1
await outside 5
wait 1.0

near door:home
await door 5
press use 0.1
await inside:home 5
wait 0.6
near shelf
wait 0.4
thanked
press use 0.1
await shelf_given 3
wait 0.6
shot 03-a-home-gives-its-shelf with inside:home
near door
wait 0.3
press use 0.1
await outside 5
wait 1.0

